    "scopeLimitations": [
      "The package and XML APIs preserve the current SwDoc paragraphs, references to the 26 materializable built-in paragraph styles and their implemented hierarchy, LibreOffice-encoded style names, document font-face declarations, alignment, title, significant whitespace, inherited/direct pooled bold, italic, and single underline formatting, plus the Standard page layout and default bullet and decimal list rules, identities, continuation blocks, and levels zero through nine; script-specific font-family differences are normalized to the Western family because the browser model exposes one synchronized family, while tables, images, fields, sections, annotations, redlines, objects, RDF, scripts, signatures, encryption, ZIP64, custom bullet glyphs, and non-decimal numbering remain explicit unsupported cases.",
      "Browser Open uses a user-selected File and Save As starts a download rather than retaining an in-place filesystem handle; export is deterministic STORE-only, DEFLATE is import-only, paragraph browser IDs are deterministically regenerated, and interoperability coverage is bounded to the three pinned LibreOffice feature_text fixtures plus locally generated semantic round trips."
    ],
